<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gitanas Nausėda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1964">1964</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gitanas Nausėda is a Lithuanian economist and politician who has been president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> since 2019. A former bank economist without party affiliation, he won the 2019 election against Ingrida Šimonytė and was re-elected in 2024. His presidency has been marked by strong support for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> and the hosting of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> summit in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilnius">Vilnius</a> in 2023.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gitanas-nauseda.jpg" alt="Gitanas Nausėda" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FinnishGovernment · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prime_Minister_Petteri_Orpo_and_President_of_Lithuania_Gitanas_Naus%C4%97da_met_in_Helsinki_2_September.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
